// ADR-0076 (#817) Phase 3: a `perform` bound via `let` inside a needing
// function's OWN body, rather than written as a bare tail expression.
//
// edp_rewrite_needing_body (and its handle-site counterpart,
// edp_rewrite_handle_body) rewrite a needing function's body by pattern-
// matching the same shapes edp_has_unsafe_construct already verified are
// safe. The two traversals used to disagree about which positions they
// visit: edp_has_unsafe_construct correctly recurses into ELet's/EAssign's
// value/RHS position (among others) when deciding eligibility, but
// edp_rewrite_needing_body's ELet/ELetMut/ELetRec/EAssign/EAssignOp cases
// only recursed into the body/continuation, silently passing the value
// position through UNCHANGED. `ask_helper`'s body here --
// `let a = perform Ask::Get; a + 1` -- puts the perform in exactly that
// skipped position: it correctly passed eligibility (nothing unsafe about
// it) but was left as a raw, un-rewritten `perform`. Since this function
// still qualifies for evidence-dict migration, its handle site gets its
// `EHandle` wrapper dropped -- so the raw perform's throw now has no
// handler left anywhere to catch it, producing an uncaught-exception
// runtime crash despite a clean compile.
//
// Found via runtime instrumentation (temporarily exporting every
// per-effect wasm exception tag by name) while investigating an unrelated
// multi-effect-row crash -- decoding the escaping exception identified it
// as the MIGRATED effect's own tag (Ask), not some foreign one, which
// pointed straight at "the needing function's own perform never got
// rewritten" rather than anything about replay/frontier interaction.
// Reproducible with a single exact-match effect, independent of the
// multi-effect investigation that led to finding it.
//
// Fixed by making edp_rewrite_needing_body (and edp_rewrite_handle_body)
// structurally mirror edp_has_unsafe_construct's traversal exactly: every
// position the eligibility check visits, the rewrite must visit too.
//
//   a == 5 (perform Ask::Get, resolved via the evidence dict)
//   main() == a + 1 == 6
effect Ask {
  Get -> Int
}

let ask_helper = () -> Int with Ask {
  let a = perform Ask::Get
  a + 1
}

export let main = () -> Int {
  handle {
    ask_helper()
  } with Ask {
    Get => resume(5)
  }
}

test "main produces its recorded value" {
  // #1571: expectation moved off a `__DATA__` tail; `vibe test --update`
  // rewrites this literal.
  inspect(main(), "6")
}
